      "content": "Thanks for the update. The count on \"citizen\" is definitely higher now, but the tracker is still flagging it as \"borderline.\" It's a bit of a tight squeeze.\n\nI think the issue is that the paragraphs are still a bit too short for the algorithm to register a high density. Could you flesh this out into a more comprehensive draft? Maybe add a paragraph about the environmental impact or the sustainability of the park's landscaping? \n\nIt really needs to hit a much higher number for that specific word to get past the threshold, but please try to keep it natural. If it starts feeling like you're just forcing the word in where it doesn't belong, the council will definitely notice. Just try to weave it in more thoroughly throughout the new sections.",
